DESCRIPTION >
    History backfill for events_deductions_hourly_mv (deployed with BACKFILL skip). Fills the window
    before the MV's forward-materialization seam, in bounded half-open [start_date, end_date) chunks
    on on-demand compute
    (tb copy run events_deductions_hourly_mv_backfill --on-demand-compute --param start_date=... --param end_date=...).
    SQL mirrors events_deductions_hourly_mv_pipe EXACTLY (same ARRAY JOIN + JSON decode + GROUP BY)
    so backfilled rows are identical to forward-materialized ones.

    Chunk sizing: unlike events_customer_hourly_mv_backfill this DOES fan out (one row per deduction
    before the hourly GROUP BY) and pays a double JSONExtract per field per row, so start with ~1-day
    chunks on prod-scale months and widen only if runs come back fast.

    Seam safety: MergeTree does NOT dedup — keep every end_date <= the MV's actual promote time
    (capture it empirically: min(hour) once forward events land), else overlapping hours double-count.

    Backfill ALL history: custom_range is unbounded, so any date can be queried. The effective
    floor is data existence, not a serving window — deductions were first written to events around
    May 2026, so earlier chunks copy zero rows by construction. scripts/backfill_deductions_mv.ts
    automates the downward fill (resume from min(hour), retries, on-demand compute).

NODE migrate
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        org_id,
        env,
        customer_id,
        coalesce(entity_id, '') as entity_id,
        event_name,
        JSONExtractString(JSONExtractString(d), 'feature_id') as balance_feature_id,
        JSONExtractString(JSONExtractString(d), 'balance_id') as balance_id,
        JSONExtractString(JSONExtractString(d), 'plan_id') as plan_id,
        JSONExtractString(
            JSONExtractRaw(JSONExtractString(d), 'reset'),
            'interval'
        ) as reset_interval,
        toStartOfHour(timestamp) as hour,
        sum(JSONExtractFloat(JSONExtractString(d), 'value')) as deducted,
        count() as deduction_count
    FROM events
    ARRAY JOIN JSONExtractArrayRaw(toString(deductions), 'list') as d
    WHERE timestamp >= {{DateTime(start_date, '2026-06-01 00:00:00')}}
        AND timestamp < {{DateTime(end_date, '2026-06-02 00:00:00')}}
        AND JSONExtractString(JSONExtractString(d), 'balance_id') != ''
    GROUP BY
        org_id,
        env,
        customer_id,
        entity_id,
        event_name,
        balance_feature_id,
        balance_id,
        plan_id,
        reset_interval,
        hour

TYPE COPY
TARGET_DATASOURCE events_deductions_hourly_mv
COPY_MODE append
